---
// /circle/: the founding circle. Every name on this page comes through
// circleNames() in site/src/data/room.mjs, which returns nothing until enough
// people have consented. Never write a name into this file directly; ask a
// co-organizer to add the person to room.mjs with `consent: true`.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { room, stream, circle, circleNames, person, firstQuestion } from '../data/room.mjs';
const names = circleNames();
const founder = person('founder');
---
<Base title="The founding circle" description="The founding circle of The Commons: what members commit to, who runs The Commons, and how invitations work." nav="room">
  <div class="wrap wrap--reading">
    <div class="page-head reading">
      <p class="eyebrow">The Commons</p>
      <h1>The founding circle</h1>
      <p class="lede">The founding circle is the first group of experienced planners in <a href="/commons/">The Commons</a>. They set the tone of The Commons, bring its first problems and review its first work.</p>
    </div>

    <section class="prose reading" aria-labelledby="commit">
      <h2 id="commit">What members commit to</h2>
      <p class="note">One post or reply a month, in The Commons. Nothing about you is listed here without your sign-off. Leave any time.</p>
      <p>Your sector is enough. Your employer is optional.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>The post</strong> is anything short: a question, an answer, an observation or a link, in <a href={stream.url}>The Commons</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Calls</strong> come later, when The Commons asks for them. If they start, they run under the Chatham House rule and are not recorded.</li>
        <li><strong>Your sign-off</strong> covers your name, your sector and anything you say. Each is shown only after a written yes.</li>
        <li><strong>Leaving</strong> takes one message. Your name comes off this page in the next update.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>The rules of The Commons apply to everyone, the circle included. See <a href="/commons/#room-rules">the rules</a> and <a href="/sharing-safely/">Sharing safely</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="prose reading" aria-labelledby="co-organizers">
      <h2 id="co-organizers">Co-organizers</h2>
      <p>Co-organizers help the founder keep The Commons useful: they welcome new posters, tag posts and point good threads toward CPP pages. It is an open volunteer role, and it grows as people step forward. See <a href="/commons/#who">Who runs this</a>.</p>
      {names && names.coOrganizers.length ? (
        <ul class="pr-names">{names.coOrganizers.map((p) => <li><strong>{p.name}</strong>{p.sector && <>, {p.sector}</>}{p.topics?.length ? <>. Topics: {p.topics.join(', ')}</> : null}</li>)}</ul>
      ) : (
        <p class="pr-empty">Open. Names appear here once each person signs off.</p>
      )}
      <p>The role has duties, a term and an easy exit. See <a href="/roles/#co-organizer">Co-organizer</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="prose reading" aria-labelledby="members">
      <h2 id="members">Founding members</h2>
      <p>Each entry shows a name or handle, a sector and the topics the person reviews. An employer appears only if the member asks for it.</p>
      {names && names.members.length ? (
        <ul class="pr-names">{names.members.map((p) => <li><strong>{p.name}</strong>{p.sector && <>, {p.sector}</>}{p.topics?.length ? <>. Topics: {p.topics.join(', ')}</> : null}</li>)}</ul>
      ) : (
        <p class="pr-empty">This list stays empty until at least {circle.showNamesAt} members have signed off. No one is listed before they say yes in writing.</p>
      )}
    </section>

    {founder && (
      <section class="prose reading" aria-labelledby="founder">
        <h2 id="founder">The founder</h2>
        <p><strong>{founder.name}</strong>{founder.sector && <>, {founder.sector}</>}. Founder and steward.</p>
        <p>He started the practice and wrote the <a href="/paper/">seed paper</a>. Anacay LLC, which he co-founded, supports the practice, and says so. He is its editor and reads cpp@anacay.org. What the circle makes belongs to the community, credited by name. See <a href="/commons/#who">Who runs this</a>.</p>
      </section>
    )}

    <section class="prose reading" aria-labelledby="invitations">
      <h2 id="invitations">How invitations work</h2>
      <p>The circle grows by “one peer, one question”. Each invitation names one open problem that the person’s experience could move.</p>
      <ol>
        <li>A co-organizer or the founder picks a question from the <a href="/agenda/">agenda</a> for one person.</li>
        <li>The invitation names that question and its thread, and links this page and <a href="/sharing-safely/">Sharing safely</a>.</li>
        <li>A one-line yes is enough. The person then says what may be shown: a name or a handle, a sector, topics.</li>
        <li>Nothing appears here until that written yes.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>Not invited yet? You don’t need to be. <a href={firstQuestion()}>Post one question in The Commons</a>.</p>
      <p>Want to do more than post? Every role is listed on <a href="/roles/">Roles</a>. How editors are added is set out in <a href="/governance/">Governance</a>.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .pr-names { list-style: none; padding-left: 0; }
  .pr-names li { padding: 0.5rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--water-line); }
  .pr-empty { color: var(--ink-muted); font-style: italic; }
</style>
